---
title: 'The Cost of Perception: Why BD Startups Fail at Long-term Strategy.'
publishedAt: '2026-04-03'
pillar: bd-lens
summary: >-
  Most founders choose "feeling good" over "being right." Here is the math on
  why that leads to dissolution.
---
Perception is a poor substitute for operational integrity. In the Dhaka startup ecosystem, there is a systemic bias toward visibility over viability. 

We see founders optimizing for LinkedIn optics—raising capital on thin unit economics while burning cash on high-visibility marketing stunts. The actual math, however, tells a different story. If you build for validation in May 2026, you will not have an enterprise in May 2036. 

This note outlines why structural math must always precede brand signaling, and why doing the boring operational work is the only guaranteed edge.
